# Failing-first tests in tests/fm-crew-state-fork-budget.test.sh, on upstream-lean: attributed-run is red because a working run's read started 122 processes beyond startup against a budget of 60. held-green-ci is red at 200 against 80, five subshells per step row. parked-gate is red at 157 against 60. runs-ledger is red at 112 against 56, a subshell per ledger row. herdr-gone is red at 528 against 45, about 12 processes per retained terminal-outcome record, where each record must cost none (agent-config .agent-config-8c70c: 637 records cost ~7,800 processes a call on 10-30). The script stops at its first red budget. In tests/fm-fork-free-helpers.test.sh, test_nm_field_and_trim_helpers_match_the_pipelines, test_nm_first_line_matches_grep and test_meta_exact_value_matches_the_grep_pipeline are red because the fork-free helpers they compare do not exist. All are green after this change.
